# Strings of remote Git sides: the Start chip, the failure line of a tab and the command-line refusal.
git-remote-chip-revision = Remote Git revision · downloaded when you compare
git-remote-chip-bad-address = Only https:// addresses without a user name are supported
git-remote-unreachable = Cannot reach the server
git-remote-not-found = Repository not found, or it needs a sign-in (not supported yet)
git-remote-redirected = The server moved this repository; type its new address
git-remote-no-such-revision = The server has no such branch or tag
git-remote-too-large = The download is larger than 256 MiB
git-remote-object-too-large = A file in the download is larger than 64 MiB
git-remote-timed-out = The server took too long to answer
git-remote-broken = The server's answer could not be read
git-remote-cli-refused = Remote Git sides are typed in the window, not on the command line.